# state.pdl - every file the game may leave in its state folder, and what kind of fact it is (no ghost data, owner 2026-11-07; BOOK 02-architecture/NO-GHOST-DATA-THE-LEDGER-IS-THE-AUTHORITY-2026-11-07.md).
# FILE | name | kind | writer | regenerate_with
#   LEDGER      append-only rows; the only place a fact about the game may live
#   PROJECTION  derived from a ledger by the verb named in regenerate_with (it must be a VERB in verbs.pdl); safe to delete, rewritten byte for byte
#   CONFIG      an input the game reads and never writes (rulesets/default/*.pdl live beside the game, not in state/)
#   PREFERENCE  a user's choice about the window (never read by the rules, never changes an outcome)
# `game_core ... audit` fails on any file in the state folder that is not declared here (a GHOST), and on a PROJECTION whose regenerating verb does not exist.
FILE | ledger.txt | LEDGER     | every verb that moves the game, and seat (game_core) | -
FILE | ui.txt     | PROJECTION | game_core ui                                          | ui
FILE | level.pdl | CONFIG | game_core play of Teario-Make (the level being edited, copied when the author pressed play; read by this game, never written by it; its text is in the rules hash of the run and its hash in Make's play row) | -
